---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Hop for business — connectivity without infrastructure"
  description="Run on Hop's managed delay-tolerant mesh backbone, or stand up a private fleet of your own. Built for events, field operations, maritime, rural, and response — where the network can't be assumed."
  path="/business"
>
  <!-- hero -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">For business</div>
      <h1>Connectivity that doesn't <span class="grad">depend on connectivity.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        When the network is congested, absent, or down, your product still has to work.
        Hop's mesh carries sealed messages device to device and bridges them across the
        world the moment any node touches the internet. Run on our managed backbone, or
        a private fleet of your own.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#contact">Talk to us</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/pricing/">See pricing</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- where it fits -->
  <section class="band band-soft">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">Where Hop earns its keep</div>
        <h2>Built for the places the network isn't.</h2>
        <p>Anywhere people and devices outnumber the infrastructure connecting them,
           a Hop mesh turns the crowd itself into the network.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <div class="card"><div class="ic">🎪</div><h3>Events &amp; venues</h3><p>Stadiums and festivals where 50,000 phones crush the cell network. Hop relays peer to peer instead of fighting for a tower.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><div class="ic">🛰️</div><h3>Field operations</h3><p>Crews, sensors, and assets spread past coverage. Data hops back to whichever node has a link, then bridges home.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><div class="ic">⚓</div><h3>Maritime &amp; transit</h3><p>Ships, fleets, and remote routes with intermittent satellite. Messages queue and deliver on the next window — eventually, reliably.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><div class="ic">🏔️</div><h3>Rural &amp; remote</h3><p>Communities past the last tower. People become the network for each other, and one online device connects the whole island.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><div class="ic">🆘</div><h3>Response &amp; resilience</h3><p>When infrastructure fails, a Hop mesh keeps standing — no central server to lose, sealed end to end.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><div class="ic">🏭</div><h3>Industrial &amp; campus</h3><p>Sites where wiring every corner is impractical. Devices relay through each other across the floor or the yard.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- managed backbone value -->
  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid-2" style="align-items:center; gap:40px;">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">The managed backbone</div>
          <h2>A global mesh you don't have to operate.</h2>
          <p class="mt-s">Hop's hosted backbone is a region-aware relay fleet with durable
             mailboxes in every region. It absorbs the carry-and-forward your phones can't,
             routes only to regions with live subscribers, and bridges islands across
             oceans — so one internet leg becomes one very long hop.</p>
          <ul class="checks">
            <li>Scale-to-zero — capacity when you need it, nothing when you don't.</li>
            <li>Region-aware routing — no wasted egress to empty regions.</li>
            <li>Durable mailboxes — messages survive until the recipient reappears.</li>
            <li>Sealed throughout — the backbone relays ciphertext it cannot read.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="grid-2" style="gap:14px;">
          <div class="card lit"><div class="ic">🔐</div><h3>Keyed access</h3><p>Every connection carries a signed access key. Anonymous traffic can't even reach your fleet.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><div class="ic">📊</div><h3>Metered &amp; attributed</h3><p>Usage is measured per tenant on the sealed envelope — volume, not content.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><div class="ic">🌐</div><h3>Anycast entrance</h3><p>One name, many regions. Devices land on the nearest node automatically.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><div class="ic">🧱</div><h3>Private fleets</h3><p>Run the same backbone on your own infrastructure, fully isolated.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- two ways to run -->
  <section class="band band-soft">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">Two ways to run</div>
        <h2>Hosted, or your own.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-2">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="ic">☁️</div>
          <h3>Managed backbone</h3>
          <p>Use Hop's global fleet with a free tier to start and usage-based pricing as
             you grow. Keyed access, per-tenant metering, regional reliability — and
             nothing to operate.</p>
          <p class="mt-s"><a class="link-go" href="/pricing/">See pricing →</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="ic">🏢</div>
          <h3>Private fleet &amp; licensing</h3>
          <p>For products outside the FSL's non-compete terms, or deployments that must
             stay on your own infrastructure: a commercial license, a private relay
             fleet, and support for mission-critical operation.</p>
          <p class="mt-s"><a class="link-go" href="#contact">Talk to us →</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- contact -->
  <section class="cta-band" id="contact">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Tell us where your network ends.</h2>
      <p>We'll help you figure out whether the managed backbone, a private fleet, or a
         commercial license fits — and what it would take to ship.</p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:hello@hopme.sh">hello@hopme.sh</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/pricing/">See pricing</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
